## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions

### What is Samsung FRP Hijacker?

Samsung FRP Hijacker is a Windows-based Samsung servicing utility associated with older Galaxy devices and functions such as device detection, ADB communication, and certain maintenance workflows.

### Is Samsung FRP Hijacker designed for Windows?

Yes. It is described as a Windows desktop utility rather than an Android application.

### Does it support every Samsung phone?

No. Compatibility depends on the exact Samsung model, Android version, security patch, bootloader configuration, and tool version.

### Does the tool use ADB?

Yes. ADB-related functions are among the capabilities associated with FRP Hijacker on compatible devices.

### Is FRP the same as a normal screen lock?

No. FRP is a separate Android security mechanism associated with Google-account verification after certain factory-reset scenarios.

### Can modern Samsung phones use older FRP Hijacker versions?

Not necessarily. Older methods may be incompatible with newer Android versions and security patches.

### Should I back up a Samsung phone before servicing?

Yes. Whenever possible, create a backup before performing maintenance or recovery operations that could affect device data.

### Is authorization important when using FRP-related tools?

Yes. Security-sensitive servicing should only be performed on devices you own or have explicit authorization to repair.

